    <Description>This package uses an executable created via Dell Command Configure to enable Secure Boot in the BIOS settings.

Note: Executable may throw an error while setting the MSUefiCA option. Needs further testing; no solutions online have been found so far. Executable seems to be able to set the SecureBoot option just fine, though.

Because PDQ expects logs to be named "output.log", not Dell's variation, no flags will make the deployment run indefinitely. Setting the flag /nolog will prevent this, but prevents us from seeing the actual log file.
Setting a custom log name with /l=".\output.log" fixes the problem, but reveals that Dell makes the installer return code 0 even if it fails! Thanks, Dell.</Description>
